{"title":"1968 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 10th <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a> 1968 in USSR. \n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that there is one and only one triangle whose side lengths are consecutive integers, and one of whose angles is twice as large as another.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all natural numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that the product of their digits (in decimal notation) is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/8/9b82e469e558f3c6930aefa3d8d692a331da7182.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 10x - 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the system of equations\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07bfbc3e9af07cc629405019dcafefd8e7e24351.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ax_1^2 + bx_1 + c = x_2\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a41aac4a2eedbae7ae523ec88d18d87c44d410f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ax_2^2 + bx_2 + c = x_3\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce26e72ef1985f46ac9b2fedbe0879501540c94c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cdots\\]\" width=\"18\" height=\"2\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/7446f53eb95598dfb0612a01007685c3183bef14.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ax_{n-1}^2 + bx_{n-1} + c = x_n\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/0/1a08d0b28d25639f127486af8b2e3f98361c180f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ax_n^2 + bx_n + c = x_1\\]\" width=\"148\" height=\"19\" />\nwith unknowns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20ca38aea3a0dc989a6070d6f67cdf1ec317d4bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, \\cdots, x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"11\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are real and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67a8181c9d9b8253bd721b620aaabc5b01f4af96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b697e4a5865fe6a50533876b0aa9abd3c311466.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta = (b - 1)^2 - 4ac$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" />. Prove that for this system\n</p><p>(a) if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/8979a4709b049b4bcbfa87d9d5a3286d0e64b526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />, there is no solution,\n</p><p>(b) if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/93008ad9888716b9f31cab7e25288dc5720325d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta = 0$\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />, there is exactly one solution,\n</p><p>(c) if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/06521e2821abce29832148c56843a25fa1c02684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />, there is more than one solution.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that in every tetrahedron there is a vertex such that the three edges meeting there have lengths which are the sides of a triangle.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> be a real-valued function defined for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that, for some positive constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c8b3bbc8a56354c4a9940dfe4076f5dad29e31a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x + a) = \\frac{1}{2} + \\sqrt{f(x) - (f(x))^2}\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"37\" />\nholds for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>(a) Prove that the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is periodic (i.e., there exists a positive number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2eb26d908eccc14446c78696ac81b7796096f518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x + b) = f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />).\n</p><p>(b) For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d02444a59b917b64e8bd0963b88712fc7fa0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, give an example of a non-constant function with the required properties.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For every natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, evaluate the sum\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab23b66f352367a017f0e97492955f7eababefb9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k = 0}^\\infty\\bigg[\\frac{n + 2^k}{2^{k + 1}}\\bigg] = \\Big[\\frac{n + 1}{2}\\Big] + \\Big[\\frac{n + 2}{4}\\Big] + \\cdots + \\bigg[\\frac{n + 2^k}{2^{k + 1}}\\bigg] + \\cdots\\]\" width=\"454\" height=\"48\" />\n(The symbol <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bceb7b14e55d33a8bca29b7863ad3cdae95afce4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the greatest integer not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO\" title=\"1968 IMO\">1968 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1968\">IMO 1968 Problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO\" title=\"1968 IMO\">1968 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO\" title=\"1967 IMO\">1967 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO\" title=\"1969 IMO\">1969 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017084907\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 177/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 836/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5064/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.679      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.679      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8938:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017084907 and revision id 143782. Rendering was triggered because: page-view